#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:6
#: 8ec6a62b2fe74b3a98fb240cd3cce5a5
msgid "Battery Voltage Compensation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:8
#: 0afbf999c8bf46cdb85805617bddc6c5
msgid "As a flight progresses the battery voltage will gradually lower as power is consumed. This affects the maximum climb rate, and the cruising speed in systems with no airpeed sensor. Plane provides two mechanisms to cope with this, one for forward motor(s) and another for VTOL motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:11
#: 9787dbc0662c42199ffcaa2701f6283d
msgid "Forward Motor Compensation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:13
#: 41624fb597b64a66b62b35947df36dfb
msgid "This is provided using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:15
#: 5d0d80eb9f414dc79b03dec6e64b4b7d
msgid ":ref:`FWD_BAT_VOLT_MAX<FWD_BAT_VOLT_MAX>`: This sets the voltage from which lower voltages will result in compensating the actual applied forward throttle upwards. A value of \"0\", disables this function. Setting this to 4.2V * number of cells is a good value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:16
#: 9aef9a7acec24fc3829383c99934a00b
msgid ":ref:`FWD_BAT_VOLT_MIN<FWD_BAT_VOLT_MIN>`: Sets the lower limit at which throttle compensation will be done to prevent dragging the battery down excessively due to increased throttle scaling. Setting this to 3.3V * number of cells is a good value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:17
#: 4269196a7cd347a8814bd724d4781a44
msgid ":ref:`FWD_BAT_IDX<FWD_BAT_IDX>`: Determines which battery monitor voltage is used (index 0-9). Index \"3\" corresponds to Battery Monitor 4, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:19
#: aa780286b38149aba733ab8fa91016e9
msgid "For battery voltages below :ref:`FWD_BAT_VOLT_MAX<FWD_BAT_VOLT_MAX>`, before the throttle value that the autopilot determines should be output is applied, it is scaled by a ratio of the this parameter versus the measured voltage. This allows all modes (except MANUAL, which never has this applied) to maintain roughly constant cruise speeds at a given throttle stick position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:21
#: c04020ea9d8c4d65982a1920b9906aa8
msgid "If an airspeed sensor is used and healthy, then for speed controlled modes, such as CRUISE and AUTO, it will determine the throttle required instead. However, the :ref:`THR_MAX<THR_MAX>` and :ref:`THR_MIN<THR_MIN>` are compensated in all modes except MANUAL, allowing speed controlled modes greater range of actual throttle control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:23
#: 9c56694f4a024077a3d597de809bc583
msgid ":ref:`FWD_BAT_VOLT_MIN<FWD_BAT_VOLT_MIN>` sets a lower limit on compensation to prevent excessive sag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:26
#: 18a693084d2448f79726baee45e421ae
msgid "Throttle Cutoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:28
#: b34a1cc09bfb45aabef175e33de5d339
msgid ":ref:`FWD_BAT_THR_CUT<FWD_BAT_THR_CUT>` parameter provides a low resting voltage cutoff of power to the forward motor as designated by :ref:`FWD_BAT_IDX<FWD_BAT_IDX>` to prevent losing power to any other circuitry (including the flight controller and servos if powered from this battery). The default value of \"0\" disables this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:31
#: 2d3fa33789fd49efbafbe05387c23ac2
msgid "QuadPlane VTOL Motor Compensation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:33
#: ba8a6d3d7a1b4b6f9e9a4bc75286211d
msgid "This is provided using in a similar manner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:35
#: 93e5cca714cc4abe82cb9999d6934f6a
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX>`: This sets the voltage from which lower voltages will result in compensating the actual applied VTOL motors throttle upwards. A value of \"0\", disables this function. Setting this to 4.2V * number of cells is a good value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:36
#: 84578da2f20a422daf1948c8f9191c82
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>`: Sets the lower limit at which throttle compensation will be done to prevent dragging the battery down excessively due to increased throttle scaling. Setting this to 3.3V * number of cells is a good value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:37
#: 0c71736860ac454ba284b61d003789c5
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_IDX<Q_M_BAT_IDX>`: Determines which battery monitor voltage is used (index 0-9). Index \"3\" corresponds to Battery Monitor 4, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:39
#: eecc8e7d421c473da7a2799f1a8ae9bd
msgid "If :ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX>` is non-zero, then voltage compensation is applied to throttle to offset battery voltage variations on thrust as above for the forward motor(s)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/battery-voltage-compensation.rst:41
#: ab80710a491b45539a11e1f9917cee45
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>` sets a lower limit on battery voltage sag by predicting the throttle value that would cause this, using an estimate of battery internal resistance calculated during flight. It will limit current applied to the VTOL motors to prevent this from occurring. If :ref:`Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX<Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX>` is also non-zero, then it will use the lower of the two limits, the one set by :ref:`Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX<Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX>` or predicted internally using :ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>` as the minimum voltage sag target."
msgstr ""
